comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-27T22:25:14.902Z",codex-agent,"Reviewing import ownership, the gated repeat check, and closeout before adding a native related edge from the mirror."
  "2026-11-27T22:25:29.054Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced on main with a real non-git tracker: a tagged in-progress Chore plus an open GitHub issue creates the mirror and neither item has a dependency. The pinned SDK provides undirected, non-ordering related relationships. Write the source edge on the mirror only so the citing item and its history stay byte-identical."
  "2026-11-27T22:34:51.655Z",codex-agent,Separate changelog follow-up filed as unbraind/pm-changelog#390 for a single release entry when a mirror and related delivery close in the same release. Verified the pinned host projects the native related edge in full get and deps context. Project-wide context has no association projection or extension section registration.
  "2026-11-27T22:38:23.809Z",codex-agent,The new edge is written on the mirror via the SDK dep update. The pending replay and refresh paths use the same plan. Verified native deps context and full get. Project context can surface the linking activity; persistent association projection is tracked as pm-github-pasp.
  "2026-11-27T22:41:31.328Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof with only the reference planner disabled: 10 distinct assertions failed across first import, multi-citation, closed-mirror backfill, closeout, refresh, original-plan recovery, gated PR text and packed consumers. With only existing-edge recognition disabled, 4 repeat and reverse-edge tests failed. Restored the implementation and rebuilt before running the linked acceptance command."
  "2026-11-27T22:41:32.698Z",codex-agent,"Linked pm test acceptance passed all 11 tests. Packed npm and native Bun each exercised JSON and TOON preview, apply, repeat and native reads. The closeout fixture closed two cited delivery items while the mirror stayed open."
  "2026-11-27T22:44:35.955Z",codex-agent,"The shared checkout's whole-object privacy audit found two pre-existing unapproved commit identities. Both objects are absent from this branch ancestry, origin remote-tracking refs and tags. Use a fresh clone of the candidate for the unchanged privacy gate."
  "2026-11-27T23:07:18.846Z",codex-agent,"Targeted Node run used 73 files and executed 1984 tests. Passed 1982, with the two repository-wide privacy tests affected by unrelated local-only identities. The exact committed candidate is checked in a clean clone. Minimum SDK packed acceptance, identity inventory, build, typecheck, test typecheck and lint passed. Strict tracker health passed with isolated user configuration."
  "2026-11-27T23:23:14.447Z",codex-agent,Rebased without conflict after pm-github#301 merged at 6229d64. The feature patch was unchanged. Regenerated ownership inventory anchors for the merged workflow and reran the affected workflow and documentation gates.
  "2026-11-27T23:31:51.442Z",codex-agent,"First pushed head passed Node 22 and CodeQL. Node 26 CI reported uncovered linker branches and lines. Added real SDK tests for a citation changed inside the mutation guard and an unavailable mirror, plus legacy projection cases. Both tests failed in a disposable copy with only those guards disabled and passed through the linked test command after restoration. Coverage thresholds are unchanged. CI evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/46080879240"
  "2026-11-28T00:44:20.452Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 review covers three invariants: required relationship writes belong to the atomic journal, complete ownership evidence can identify legacy mirrors without a URL, and builtin-kind comparisons must tolerate unrelated workspace-defined kinds. Also testing one edge per unordered pair and first-pass planning from the whole projected batch. Main is already an ancestor of the PR head."
  "2026-11-28T00:53:59.030Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural reverts in a disposable source copy failed 2 atomic rollback/replay cases, 3 legacy import/refresh cases, 1 registered-kind case, 2 first-batch cases, and 2 reciprocal-pair cases. Reverting the history generation fence, refresh recovery receipt, or stable receipt ordering failed one additional test each. Tests keep the native SDK and tracker active."
  "2026-11-28T01:27:24.567Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 targeted suite ran 1978 tests across 72 files. The 1977 passing cases included the gated workflow and minimum SDK. The packed test exposed that the SDK bulk update reserves its activity message for the recovery marker. Expanded the consumer matrix to confirm the original plain activity label and the exact atomic activity event backed by the typed history patch, for npm and Bun in JSON and TOON. All 6 packed projection tests passed on the rerun. Durable named atomic activity projection remains a host follow-up."
  "2026-11-28T01:54:18.543Z",codex-agent,"Round 1 head b2e3ee0 passed exact CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/46093325963: 2255 tests each on Node 22 and Node 26, exact four-dimensional coverage across 36 authored modules, 11 Bun smoke tests. Merged main at 37b235d after pm-github#298 landed. Preserved the source freshness fence, comment receipts and real no-op gate alongside journaled citation mutations and replay receipts."
  "2026-11-28T02:09:16.839Z",codex-agent,"Greptile thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM68-76D identified inconsistent mirror eligibility. A shared predicate now applies to ordinary import, refresh preview and apply, and persisted-plan replay. The two new real-tracker tests fail against the previous code because preview emits unwanted edges for an explicit link-only record and an importer-created provider owner. The control full mirror is selected, the curated owner remains unlinked, and the tests exercise plain and atomic apply, unchanged citing files, and byte-identical repeat refresh."
  "2026-11-28T02:10:26.120Z",codex-agent,"The targeted citation suite passed all 16 cases after the mirror-eligibility fix, including both new revert-sensitive refresh cases."
  "2026-11-28T03:36:24.779Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 thread PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM68_Wfd concerns stale mirror eligibility. Every citation write must recheck the current mirror under the native lock, including rows in retained transactions."
  "2026-11-28T03:43:17.987Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert in a disposable copy: the same current test file against the previous implementation failed all six cases through missing rejection. Plain apply, retained citation-only replay and retained source-update replay each accepted both a persisted link-only marker and a newly declared provider owner. The shared locked guard rejects before an earlier source row can erase the evidence. All 13 focused tests passed with the fix, including normal links and interrupted replay."
  "2026-11-28T03:58:55.183Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 passed the 6 PM-linked cases and all 1149 targeted tests across 33 files, including packed npm and Bun, the declared minimum SDK, owner consistency, inventory and gated repeat publication. Typecheck, build, test build, lint and docstrings passed. Both production files, the regression test and the updated docs are linked on this item."
